This was a pretty straight-forward ascension, I suppose. My God didn't
seem very inclined to provide useful sacrifice gifts (I got Snickersnee
and Orcrist), but the RNG more than made up for it by providing me with
a bones pile containing the Gauntlets of Defense and a
randomly-generated Sword of Justice just lying around. In Vlad's tower
I found Fire Brand as well, but I was pretty happy with
double-weaponing Excalibur and the Sword of Justice.

For most of the game, I had two devas following me around, and from the
castle a Solar (summoned with a figurine). Alas, the two devas died
during the ascent, and the Solar failed to follow me through the portal
into the Astral plane.

My biggest problem was in Moloch's sanctum -- there I got hit by a
lightning bolt that exploded my wands. Unfortunately, one of those was
a wand of polymorph, so I found myself as a grey dragon for a short
time, and then as a half-naked samurai after "dying", most of whose
armor had been polymorphed into different things. I managed to not pick
up my speed boots after that -- I had assumed that the fireproof +4
levitation boots were the speed boots, but no, they were my helm of
brilliance. I got paralyzed by something there and used up an AoLS. But
after that, things were easy. The Wizard needed like four rounds of
combat to kill him. Juiblex didn't even manage to engulf me -- two hits
from Excalibur and one from Sword of Justice took him right out.

This is my second legitimate win at Slash'em.

